1|0@relationship_advice^1440865259#cujtof4:theneen$:&gt;"im not in love with you" That's all you really need to know. No amount of obsessing over it, or questioning it will change anything. It's *over.* Please do not constantly ask her about it, either. She told you how she felt. Whether or not those reasons are "good enough" for you is irrelevant. They're her reasons, and they're valid. Leave her be.
1|0@relationship_advice^1440869172#cujvqk7:Thereg123$:Please don't make me look like I am nagging her when it's been 3 weeks and we haven't talked about it for over 2 and a half. People deserve closure, especially when they still care for one another after a break up, otherwise they will go insane. She asked me what her faults were and visa versa. "Im not in love with you anymore" is just a excuse that has reasons behind it, and behold she had reasons.
1|0@relationship_advice^1440893581#cuk8j28:theneen$:Your whole response is b.s. No one "deserves" closure, and no one owes you any. That's not how life works. If you go insane over this, you have way bigger problems than just not getting "closure." Also, "I'm not in love with you" is completely valid on it's own. It's not an excuse, it is a legitimate sentiment. You don't get to dismiss that just because you don't want to accept it.
1|0@relationship_advice^1440905799#cukeqby:Thereg123$:Lol ok man/gal. If you believe its not disrespectful to trash a long term relationship without any details and then peace out right afterwards you need to stop giving "advice".
0|0@relationship_advice^1440908001#cukfrfc:theneen$:No. You need to quit being a baby. It's over. Ending a relationship is not disrespectful. Not sticking around to coddle you after she's ended it is not disrespectful. It's called **moving on.** The relationship no longer exists. She is no longer obligated to do anything for you, and that includes giving explanations that you're demanding from her. She gave you all the details she wanted to give, you have no right to hound her for more or make her rehash what she's already told you. *That is harrassment.* Leave her alone. 
